      ],
      "message": "cmake, crypto: Use `-msse4.1` instead of `-msse4` for x86 SHA-NI\n\n`-msse4` is merely a synonym for `-msse4.2` in both GCC and Clang, but\nit is not accepted by the clang-cl frontend. Furthermore, the x86\nSHA-NI code uses only SSE4.1 intrinsics and no SSE4.2 ones.\n\nReplace `-msse4` with `-msse4.1` to resolve both issues.\n\nThe absence of SSE4.2 usage can be verified by building with\n`-DAPPEND_CXXFLAGS=-mno-sse4.2`.",
